WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
This lifecycle approach identifies four
specific phases where ethics must be

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.940
integrated. The initial design, technical
development, active deployment,

3
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.200
and ongoing use and monitoring.

4
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.380
Within these phases, the committee's
evaluation is defined by three

5
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.840
uncompromising structural boundaries.

6
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.620
The first boundary addresses methodological
risks, scrutinizing the specific

7
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:29.260
methods used to protect participant
privacy and verify data anonymization.

8
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:34.720
The second boundary evaluates safety,
assessing serious risks to the physical,

9
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.680
psychological, or broader interests of
subjects.

10
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:42.480
The third boundary enforces legal
compliance, ensuring adherence to local data

11
00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.100
protection and intellectual property laws.

12
00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:49.500
Effective evaluation requires tracking a
project across both axes,

13
00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.020
following its progress through the
development lifecycle, and holding it

14
00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.080
against these three compliance boundaries.
